# Hidden Settings row publishes no accessibility nodes, keeps its draft, and takes no focus.
# Hiding here is the arrangement editor's Hide on the Theme row (the first row), which the
# product parks while keeping its session. Run headed with a fresh TURNSTONE_ROOT, a
# TURNSTONE_CAPTURE_DIR and TURNSTONE_A11Y_PUBLIC_FIXTURE_RECEIPT=1, then:
#   scripts/check-settings-hidden-a11y.py <capture dir>
# The Hide click is by window position (resize 1180 950, maximized pane): a role selector for
# "Hide" matches every row's button and did not act on the first. Show is unambiguous once
# one row is hidden.
settle 20
key escape
resize 1180 950
open mere://settings-reactive
settle 10
act id:pane:settings
settle 5
assert pane turnstone.settings
act Maximize pane
settle 4
click surface:settings .radio Merely
settle 3
click surface:settings role:button Edit arrangement
settle 3
record-uxtree visible
click-at 345 311
settle 4
record-uxtree hidden
click surface:settings role:button Show
settle 4
record-uxtree restored
click-at 345 311
settle 4
click surface:settings role:button Reload saved
settle 3
record-uxtree h00
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree h01
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree h02
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree h03
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree h04
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree h05
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree h06
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree h07
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree h08
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree h09
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree h10
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree h11
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree h12
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree h13
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree h14
log hidden-row snapshots recorded; run scripts/check-settings-hidden-a11y.py on the capture dir
